diff --git a/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md b/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md
index 7e1c120d77..00672b8966 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md
+++ b/apps/desktop/DESIGN.md
@@ -466,15 +466,13 @@ from their root base tokens; do not multiply the global tokens or nest CSS zoom.
   6px reads as a rendering hiccup. `stalled` stays hollow and still on purpose. The row background, border and title
   stay still, and the motion is the same primitive the pane tabs and the session
   switcher already render.
-- **Inline code is classified, and the chip inverts per mode.** The string alone
-  decides the kind (`src/lib/inline-code.ts`): shell command, filesystem path,
-  model id, token/hash — four hues, each carried by a glyph as much as a colour,
-  so it survives grayscale and colour-blindness. The glyph is a `::before` mask,
-  never a child element: an `<i>` inside a code span rides along into a copy, and
-  inline code exists to be copied. Unclassified spans stay a plain chip — black
-  with white type in light mode, WHITE with dark type in dark mode (the owner's
-  pick: a printed label on a near-black page). Ink is declared per mode; a green
-  that reads on `#191919` is muddy on white.
+- **Inline code is ONE chip, inverted per mode.** No classification: a command,
+  a path and an identifier all read the same, because colouring them turned the
+  paragraph into confetti and fought the prose. Light mode is a black chip with
+  white type; dark mode is the inverse — white chip, dark type — so a command
+  reads as a printed label on the near-black page rather than a grey highlight.
+  The face is the app's mono stack: bundled **IBM Plex Mono** (OFL, latin
+  subset), falling through to JetBrains Mono and then the system mono fonts.
 - **No empty-slot reaction affordance.** A message never draws a reaction
   control on its own: the ☺ appeared the moment the pointer crossed a turn, which
   read as clutter under the sent bubble. `data-slot="aui_msg-reactions"` renders
